<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.tradingbotapp.ftmo</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>-lc</string>
        <string>/Users/kaloyanivanov/TradingBotApp/ftmo_runner.sh</string>
    </array>

    <!-- NOT INSTALLED BY DEFAULT. This file is tracked so the schedule is
         reviewable, but nothing loads it automatically. Install with:
             cp com.tradingbotapp.ftmo.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
             launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.tradingbotapp.ftmo.plist
         and remove it with `launchctl unload` on the same path.

         ONE firing per day, at 01:15 local. The agreed FTMO cadence is a
         DAILY rebalance with multi-day holds, and the signal is a 20-day
         forecast off daily bars — running it hourly would re-decide a
         20-day view 24 times a day and pay spread on sampling noise each
         time. This project has already measured what that costs: Kronos's
         per-run spread moves top-N membership when names sit close
         together, and the rotation margin suppresses the churn rather than
         making the re-decisions meaningful.

         01:15 local (EEST/EET, UTC+3/+2) is 00:15 or 23:15 in Europe/Prague,
         i.e. shortly after the FTMO day boundary that ftmo_rules uses. That
         ordering matters: ftmo_runner.advance_state() rolls the day-start
         balance and the trailing high-water mark off the previous day's
         CLOSING balance, so firing just after the boundary means the roll
         happens on settled numbers.

         It deliberately does NOT avoid FTMO's 23:55-00:05 Moscow maintenance
         window by construction — 01:15 local is well clear of it, but the
         venue stays the authority either way: a MARKET_CLOSED rejection is
         journalled and the run ends without placing anything, which is the
         correct outcome rather than something to schedule around. -->
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <array>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>1</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>15</integer></dict>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/kaloyanivanov/TradingBotApp/ftmo_launchd.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/kaloyanivanov/TradingBotApp/ftmo_launchd.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
